.TH FSTAT 1.SH NAMEfstat \- show a file's descriptor.SH SYNOPSIS\fBfstat\fR[\-s] file ....SH DESCRIPTION\fBfstat\fRprints what the RBF file descriptor sector records about each file: itsowner, attributes, creation and modification dates and length, indecimal and hexadecimal.\fB\-s\fRadds the segment list -- the starting sector and length of each pieceof the file on the disk, and how many pieces there are.  It calls itself\fBFStat\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOssl, attr, dir